Overlay patch 0032 (reference 0027 regenerated): audio bridge null-CHAIN
guards. Recurring reference Vision Pro SEGV (crash.txt, twice):
AudioPlayerBuffered+32 on OTRAudio_Thread — the bridge null-checks the
PLAYER but not the chain; Context()->GetAudio() is null during
init/teardown windows and ->GetAudioPlayer() on it faults. Guard the
chain in every bridge function the audio thread can hit (all six here).

Still required at upstream 5.0.0, which is worth stating plainly because
the file now LOOKS guarded: 5.0.0 added `audio == nullptr` and
`!audio->IsInitialized()` early-outs, but both test the PLAYER, and the
faulting dereference is `GetAudio()->GetAudioPlayer()` — evaluated before
either check can run. The chain guard is what keeps a null GetAudio()
from faulting. 5.0.0 also closed the old fork delta by moving this file
to GetRawInstance(), so the accessor now matches the Ship of Harkinian port.

--- a/libultraship/src/libultraship/bridge/audiobridge.cpp
+++ b/libultraship/src/libultraship/bridge/audiobridge.cpp
@@ -5,7 +5,11 @@
 extern "C" {
 
 int32_t AudioPlayerBuffered() {
-    auto audio = Ship::Context::GetRawInstance()->GetAudio()->GetAudioPlayer();
+    auto sohIosCtx = Ship::Context::GetRawInstance();
+    if (sohIosCtx == nullptr || sohIosCtx->GetAudio() == nullptr) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+    auto audio = sohIosCtx->GetAudio()->GetAudioPlayer();
     if (audio == nullptr) {
         return 0;
     }
